==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=to [[suck]] [[up]]|sucks up|sucking up|sucked up}}

# To [[absorb]] fluid
#: ''The dry soil '''sucked up''' water like a sponge.''
# {{idiom}} To [[adulate]] or [[flatter]] somebody excessively, generally to obtain some personal [[benefit]] or [[favour]].
#: ''Jimmy '''sucked up''' to the English teacher hoping he would get an A.''

